# pipeline/CODEOWNERS.example — EXAMPLE ONLY. It does nothing here.
#
# In your fork copy this file to `.github/CODEOWNERS` (or `CODEOWNERS` in the
# repo root) and replace the @org/... teams with real teams or logins. Then turn
# on branch protection "Require review from Code Owners" on the base branch.
#
# Why it exists next to pipeline/ai-review.yml: the merge gate (`merge-gate`)
# enforces approvals by ROLE from the repository variables SECURITY_OWNERS,
# FINANCE_OWNERS and MAINTAINERS. CODEOWNERS is the second, GitHub-native layer
# for the same ownership — and the only layer that also protects the pipeline
# itself: a PR that edits `pipeline/` (and therefore the gate) runs with ITS
# version of the workflow, so the gate alone cannot defend its own definition.
# Keep the teams below and the three variables in sync.
#
# Later rules win over earlier ones; a path matches like .gitignore.

# Access control and the PII access log -> security owners (vars.SECURITY_OWNERS)
app/src/auth.js            @org/security
app/src/audit.js           @org/security
app/src/members.js         @org/security

# Money: late fees, kopecks, FEE_PER_DAY_KOPECKS -> finance owners (vars.FINANCE_OWNERS)
app/src/loans.js           @org/finance

# DB structure / seed data, dependencies, the test suite -> maintainers (vars.MAINTAINERS)
app/src/db.js              @org/maintainers
app/package.json           @org/maintainers
app/test/                  @org/maintainers

# The review rules and the pipeline itself: every change is a change of policy,
# reviewed by maintainers separately from feature PRs (docs/pipeline.md, threat model).
pipeline/                  @org/maintainers
review/                    @org/maintainers
.claude/                   @org/maintainers
.github/                   @org/maintainers
